WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.501
.

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:02.135 line:78%
DEMOCRATS ALWAYS GIVE THEMSELVES

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.237 line:78%
A FREE PASS.

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:07.474 line:78%
WE'LL HAVE MORE ON THIS IN PART

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:09.342 line:78%
TWO OF MY MONOLOGUE STATE.

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:10.910 line:78%
BUT FIRST THE GOVERNOR OF

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.177 line:78%
FLORIDA, RON DESANTIS, IS WITH

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.513 line:78%
US.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:15.782 line:78%
I KNOW YOU HAVEN'T SLEPT IN THE

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:17.283 line:78%
LAST 72 HOURS OR LONGER, BEEN

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:20.186 line:78%
GOING AROUND THE STATE.

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:20.587 line:78%
$100 BILLION NOW ESTIMATED IN

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:21.187 line:78%
DAMAGE.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:25.058 line:78%
DAWNING THAT'S ACCURATE?

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:34.834 line:78%
WE LOST, I THINK, THE LAST COUNT

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:36.569 line:78%
IS 68 PEOPLE DIED IN THE STORM.

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:39.039 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I DON'T KNOW IF IT'S

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.839 line:78%
ACCURATE, BUT THE LIVES LOST ARE

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:41.408 line:78%
SIGNIFICANT, BECAUSE THAT'S

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.542 line:78%
SOMETHING WE CAN'T BUILD BACK.

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:43.676 line:78%
THOSE LOSSES ARE TOUGH.

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:45.045 line:78%
THERE'S PROPERTY DAMAGE.

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:46.346 line:78%
THERE'S A SPIRIT OUT THERE,

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:47.814 line:78%
PARTICULARLY THE PEOPLE OF

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:48.715 line:78%
SOUTHWEST FLORIDA, THEY'RE READY

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.949 line:78%
TO BOUNCE BACK.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:51.317 line:78%
THEY NEED SOME HELP.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.952 line:78%
WE'RE DOWN THERE DOING IT, BUT

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.386 line:78%
THEY HAVE A LOT OF GRIT AND

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.788 line:78%
DETERMINATION.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:56.122 line:78%
I ACTUALLY WAS JUST IN ONE OF

00:00:55.121 --> 00:01:02.529 line:78%
THE SHELTERS.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:01:03.363 line:78%
I'M MEETING WITH WOMEN WHO ARE

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:05.498 line:78%
85-90 YEARS OLD WHO SURVIVED

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:07.300 line:78%
BEING IN SOME OF THE ISLANDS,

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:09.169 line:78%
AND THEY'RE TELLING THEIR

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.004 line:78%
STORIES, BASICALLY THANKING GOD,

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.905 line:78%
BUT SO THANKFUL FOR ALL THE

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:12.839 line:78%
OUTPOURING OF SUPPORT OF

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:16.576 line:78%
EVERYBODY HELPING OUR STATE.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:21.581 line:78%
SO I JUST THINK THOSE WHO HAVE

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:22.348 line:78%
EITHER DONATED TO

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.950 line:78%
FLORIDADISASTERFUND.ORG, JUST

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:25.585 line:78%
KNOW THE PEOPLE IMPACTED BY

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:28.121 line:78%
THIS, WHO LOST EVERYTHING, THEY

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:29.656 line:78%
ARE TRULY GRATEFUL FOR THE

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.390 line:78%
OUTPOURING OF SUPPORT.

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:34.627 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Sean: GOVERNOR, THEY'RE

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:36.129 line:78%
SAYING THAT SANIBEL ISLAND MAY

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:38.031 line:78%
BE UNINHABITABLE.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:38.965 line:78%
I KNOW FORT MYERS WELL.

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:40.400 line:78%
I KNOW NAPLES WELL.

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:42.235 line:78%
I CAN'T BELIEVE THE AMOUNT OF

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.204 line:78%
DAMAGE WE'RE TALKING ABOUT.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:45.939 line:78%
IT WAS A DIRECT HIT.

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:46.339 line:78%
IT DECIMATED SOME OF THESE

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:48.875 line:78%
AREAS.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:50.477 line:78%
AS OF NOW, WHERE DO YOU SEE THIS

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:52.612 line:78%
GOING IN THE FUTURE?

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:53.813 line:78%
DO YOU BELIEVE EVERYBODY IN

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:55.448 line:78%
SANIBEL, FOR EXAMPLE, WILL HAVE

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:57.851 line:78%
TO COME OFF THE ISLAND?

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.418 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, WE'RE TRYING TO AVOID

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:00.420 line:78%
THAT.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:02.355 line:78%
I JUST ANNOUNCED TODAY THAT MY

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:05.525 line:78%
DEPARTMENT OF TRANSPORTATION WE

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:07.026 line:78%
JUST PUT OUT BIDS FOR A

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:08.661 line:78%
TEMPORARY BRIDGE TO LINK THE

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:10.330 line:78%
ISLAND BACK TO THE MAINLAND.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.697 line:78%
THERE'S A CAUSEWAY THAT HAD DONE

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.198 line:78%
THAT.

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:13.066 line:78%
IT GOT SEVERED IN THREE

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.334 line:78%
DIFFERENT PLACES.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:17.370 line:78%
WE THINK WE CAN HAVE A

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:18.671 line:78%
SHORT-TERM SOLUTION TO ALLOW

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.672 line:78%
INGRESS AND EGRESS.

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:21.774 line:78%
ALSO THE SITUATION, BECAUSE THE

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:23.143 line:78%
BRIDGE WAS SEVERED, THE LOCAL

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:24.177 line:78%
UTILITY HAS NOT HAD ANYBODY

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:28.915 line:78%
LOOKING AT THE POWER SITUATION.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:31.317 line:78%
WHAT I SAID IS WE'RE GOING TO

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:32.685 line:78%
PROVIDE CHINOOK HELICOPTERS FROM

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:35.121 line:78%
THE NATIONAL GUARD TO BRING

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:36.990 line:78%
LINEMEN ON TO SANIBEL ISLAND TO

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:38.258 line:78%
INSPECT THE SUBSTATIONS, SEE

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.658 line:78%
WHAT'S DAMAGED, AND START TO

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:40.326 line:78%
PREPARE IT.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:41.928 line:78%
I THINK YOU JUST NEED TO GET

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:43.663 line:78%
PEOPLE ON THERE, AN THEY NEED TO

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:44.364 line:78%
START DOING WHAT NEEDS TO BE

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:46.399 line:78%
DONE, CLEARING ROADS.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:48.434 line:78%
WE ARE WORKING ON THE ROADS, AND

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:49.402 line:78%
ALL THAT NOW, CLEARING THE

00:02:48.535 --> 00:02:49.736 line:78%
DEBRIS, GETTING THE ELECTRICAL

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.672 line:78%
BACK UP.

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:54.474 line:78%
SO YOU'RE GOING TO SOON SEE

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:56.342 line:78%
LINEMEN BROUGHT IN BY HELICOPTER

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:57.677 line:78%
TO PLACES LIKE SANIBEL AND PINE

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.344 line:78%
ISLAND, BECAUSE WE DON'T WANT TO

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.946 line:78%
WAIT FOR THIS.

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:00.813 line:78%
WE WANT TO DO AS MUCH AS WE CAN

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:02.382 line:78%
NOW.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.417 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Sean: WHAT IS YOUR REACTION,

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:06.119 line:78%
GOVERNOR, TO THE VICE PRESIDENT,

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:07.453 line:78%
IT'S OUR LOWEST INCOME

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:09.989 line:78%
COMMUNITIES, OUR COMMUNITIES OF

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:10.990 line:78%
COLOR, THAT ARE MOST IMPACTED BY

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:13.393 line:78%
THESE EXTREME CONDITIONS.

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:16.029 line:78%
WE HAVE TO ADDRESS THIS IN A WAY

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:18.198 line:78%
THAT IS ABOUT GIVING RESOURCES

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:21.334 line:78%
BASED ON EQUITY.

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:25.104 line:78%
WHAT WAS YOUR REACTION TO THAT?

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:27.874 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I THINK SHE'S TRYING TO PLAY

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:29.209 line:78%
IDENTITY POLITICS WITH A STORM,

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:30.743 line:78%
A NATURAL DISASTER.

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:33.346 line:78%
I THINK IT'S RIDICULOUS.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:36.549 line:78%
AND HONESTLY, WE HAD THE FEMA

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:40.119 line:78%
ADMINISTRATOR IN FLORIDA WITH

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:40.486 line:78%
US, AND SHE THREW COLD WATER ON

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.988 line:78%
THAT.

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:45.124 line:78%
THAT'S NOT GOING TO HAPPEN.

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:48.728 line:78%
IT'S TOTALLY INAPPROPRIATE.

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:49.996 line:78%
YOU DON'T HAVE TO POLITICALIZE

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:51.564 line:78%
EVERY TRAGEDY IN THIS COUNTRY.

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:54.100 line:78%
PEOPLE ARE SICK OF THE NONSENSE.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:55.201 line:78%
THEY WANT PEOPLE HELPED,

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:57.503 line:78%
EVERYONE BAND TOGETHER, AND GET

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:57.870 line:78%
THE COMMUNITIES BACK ON THEIR

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:58.805 line:78%
FEET.

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:59.539 line:78%
THAT'S WHAT WE'RE DOING IN

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:01.441 line:78%
FLORIDA.

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:04.110 line:78%
SEAN, THE IMPACTS SPANNED ALL

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:06.145 line:78%
DEMOGRAPHICS, ALL INCOME LEVELS.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:07.113 line:78%
SANIBEL HAS SOME WEALTHY PEOPLE.

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:07.513 line:78%
THEY ALSO HAVE BLUE COLLAR

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:08.881 line:78%
PEOPLE.

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:12.619 line:78%
YOU HAVE OTHER COMMUNITIES,

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:13.019 line:78%
DIFFERENT RACE, DIFFERENT

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:14.053 line:78%
ETHNICITIES.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.688 line:78%
WHO CARES.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:19.525 line:78%
WE WANT TO MAKE SURE PEOPLE CAN

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:20.159 line:78%
GET ON THEIR FEET AND MOVING

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:21.494 line:78%
FORWARD AGAIN.

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.362 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Sean: AMERICA STEPS UP AND

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:24.130 line:78%
HELP FOREIGN COUNTRIES.

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:25.598 line:78%
WE STEP UP WHEN ANOTHER STATION

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.699 line:78%
HAS A SITUATION LIKE THIS.

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:27.100 line:78%
FLORIDA DESERVES THE EXACT SAME

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.135 line:78%
TREATMENT.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:31.771 line:78%
YOU'RE RIGHT IN THE SENSE THAT

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:32.205 line:78%
THIS IS A ONE IN A 500-YEAR

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:34.274 line:78%
STORM.

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:35.608 line:78%
I LOVE HOW PEOPLE TOOK OUT OF

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:37.010 line:78%
CONTEXT -- I FELT THEY TOOK IT

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:38.645 line:78%
OUT OF CONTEXT, YOUR REMARKS.

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:39.812 line:78%
YOU KNOW, UNFORTUNATELY, THERE

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:41.481 line:78%
ARE ALWAYS BAD PEOPLE THAT WILL

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:43.316 line:78%
TRY TO CAPITALIZE ON A TRAGEDY.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:45.184 line:78%
THERE ARE PEOPLE THAT WOULD GO

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:46.919 line:78%
OUT AND INVOLVE THEMSELVES IN

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:48.721 line:78%
THINGS LIKE LOOTING.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:50.089 line:78%
YOU'RE SAYING, YOU BETTER BE

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:52.025 line:78%
CAREFUL IN THIS STATE, BECAUSE

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:53.693 line:78%
PEOPLE IN THIS STATE HAVE THEIR

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:54.694 line:78%
SECOND AMENDMENT RIGHTS TO

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:56.162 line:78%
PROTECT THEIR HOMES AND FAMILY.

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:57.664 line:78%
YOU WOULD THINK THAT WAS THE

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:58.998 line:78%
MOST CONTROVERSIAL THING TO SAY.

00:04:57.864 --> 00:05:03.069 line:78%
IF ANYTHING, YOU'RE REMINDING

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:03.936 line:78%
PEOPLE NOT TO TAKE -- NOT TO

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:04.804 line:78%
TAKE ADVANTAGE OF A SITUATION

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:05.938 line:78%
LIKE THIS.

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.406 line:78%
I THOUGHT THE COMMENTS WERE

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:08.975 line:78%
PERFECTLY FINE.

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:13.246 line:78%
WHAT WAS YOUR REACTION TO THAT?

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:14.480 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, ALSO, SEAN, I TOURED

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:15.748 line:78%
THURSDAY, AFTER THE -- THE

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:18.418 line:78%
MORNING AFTER THE STORM, I WAS

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:18.751 line:78%
IN PUNTA GORDA, IN CHARLOTTE

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:19.886 line:78%
COUNTY.

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:21.087 line:78%
THEY HAD ALL THEIR BUSINESSES

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:25.792 line:78%
BOARDED UP DOWNTOWN.

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:28.027 line:78%
A LOT OF THE PLACARDS I SAW, THE

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:30.129 line:78%
WOOD, THEY SPRAY-PAINTED, YOU

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:32.665 line:78%
LOOT, WE SHOOT, SENDING THE

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:35.468 line:78%
MESSAGE THAT LAWLESSNESS WOULD

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:37.236 line:78%
NOT BE TOLERATED.

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:39.572 line:78%
WHEN THESE SITUATIONS HAPPEN, IT

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:40.907 line:78%
DESCENDS INTO LAWLESSNESS, LIKE

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:41.674 line:78%
IT HAS AFTER SOME OTHER

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:45.578 line:78%
DISASTERS WE'VE SEEN IN AMERICA

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:47.547 line:78%
AND OTHER COUNTRIES, THE WHOLE

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:49.749 line:78%
SOCIAL FABRIC STARTS TO DECAY.

00:05:47.647 --> 00:05:51.718 line:78%
WE HAVE TO DRAW A CLEAR LINE IN

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:55.955 line:78%
THE SAND AT THE BEGINNING.

00:05:51.818 --> 00:06:01.561 line:78%
IRNOT GOING TO CAPITALIZE OFF

00:05:56.055 --> 00:06:02.095 line:78%
PEOPLE'S SUFFERING, RANSACK OR

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:04.163 line:78%
LOOT.

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:04.964 line:78%
THEY'VE CAUGHT SOME LOOTERS, BUT

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:06.399 line:78%
FORTUNATELY SINCE WE'VE BEEN SO

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:08.434 line:78%
STRONG ON IT YOU HAVEN'T SEEN IT

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:09.035 line:78%
LIKE THE AFTERMATH OF OTHER

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.470 line:78%
NATURAL DISASTERS.

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:12.972 line:78%
WE'RE PROUDLY A LAW AND ORDER

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:14.574 line:78%
STATE, PROUDLY A STATE THAT LETS

00:06:13.072 --> 00:06:15.842 line:78%
INDIVIDUAL FLORIDIANS DEFEND

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:16.943 line:78%
THEMSELVES, THEIR FAMILIES AND

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:17.443 line:78%
THEIR HOMES.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.811 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Sean: YEAH.

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:20.713 line:78%
NOW FOR PEOPLE THAT WANT TO

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:22.382 line:78%
HELP, IT'S AT THE BOTTOM OF YOUR

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:23.182 line:78%
SCREEN,

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:24.851 line:78%
FLORIDADISASTERFUND.ORG.

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:26.753 line:78%
I KNOW YOU'VE HAD A BUSY, YOU

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:27.120 line:78%
KNOW, WEEK THE LAST WEEK,

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:28.521 line:78%
GOVERNOR.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.622 line:78%
OUR THOUGHTS AND PRAYERS ARE

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:30.390 line:78%
WITH OUR FRIENDS IN THE FREE

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.457 line:78%
STATE OF FLORIDA.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:32.592 line:78%
THANK YOU FOR BEING WITH US.

